{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואהבך", :translit "v'ahavkha", :gloss "and He will love you"} {:he "בזכות אברהם", :translit "bizkhut avraham", :gloss "in the merit of Abraham"} {:he "זרע אברהם אוהבי", :translit "zerakh avraham ohevai", :gloss "the seed of Abraham My lover"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word-linking: ואהבך echoes the root א-ה-ב applied to Abraham in Isaiah 41:8."}], :frame {:text "Abraham is identified by the root א-ה-ב ('love') in Isaiah 41:8: 'the seed of Abraham My lover (אוהבי).' Ba'al HaTurim links that designation to the promise 'and He will love you (ואהבך)' in Deuteronomy 7:13, establishing that the divine love promised there flows through Abraham's merit.", :sources ["Isaiah 41:8" "Deuteronomy 7:13"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וברכך", :translit "uvarkhekha", :gloss "and He will bless you"} {:he "בזכות יצחק", :translit "bizkhut yitzchak", :gloss "in the merit of Isaac"} {:he "ויברך אלהים את יצחק", :translit "vayevarekh elohim et yitzchak", :gloss "and Elohim blessed Isaac"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word-linking: וברכך shares the root ב-ר-ך with Genesis 25:11's blessing of Isaac."}], :frame {:text "Isaac is the object of an explicit divine blessing in Genesis 25:11: 'And Elohim blessed Isaac.' Ba'al HaTurim links that verse to the promise 'and He will bless you (וברכך)' in Deuteronomy 7:13, establishing that the blessing promised there flows through Isaac's merit.", :sources ["Genesis 25:11" "Deuteronomy 7:13"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והרבך", :translit "v'hirbekha", :gloss "and He will multiply you"} {:he "בזכות יעקב", :translit "bizkhut ya'akov", :gloss "in the merit of Jacob"} {:he "פרה ורבה", :translit "peru urvu", :gloss "be fruitful and multiply"} {:he "ויתן לך האלהים מטל השמים", :translit "v'yiten lekha ha-elohim mital ha-shamayim", :gloss "and may the Elohim give you of the dew of heaven"} {:he "שיהיו לך כל אותן הברכות", :translit "she-yihyu lekha kol otan ha-berakhot", :gloss "that all those blessings should be yours"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Letter-linking: the phrase from Deut 7:13 starting at והרבך begins with vav and ends with kaf, matching Genesis 27:28 (ויתן...וכל) which also begins with vav and ends with kaf."}], :frame {:text "God commands Jacob directly in Genesis 35:11: 'be fruitful and multiply (פרו ורבו).' Separately, Isaac's blessing of Jacob in Genesis 27:28 opens with vav (ויתן) and the blessing unit closes with kaf (וכל). Ba'al HaTurim observes that the segment of Deuteronomy 7:13 beginning at והרבך likewise opens with vav and closes with kaf (the kaf-suffix at the end of the verse's last word). This shared acrostic frame binds all of Isaac's blessings onto Israel.", :sources ["Genesis 35:11" "Genesis 27:28" "Deuteronomy 7:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word-linking: ואהבך echoes the root א-ה-ב applied to Abraham in Isaiah 41:8.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Word-linking: וברכך shares the root ב-ר-ך with Genesis 25:11's blessing of Isaac.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Letter-linking: the phrase from Deut 7:13 starting at והרבך begins with vav and ends with kaf, matching Genesis 27:28 (ויתן...וכל) which also begins with vav and ends with kaf.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:02.973806155Z", :model "glm-5.2"}